& [CorrectionReview] passes
  + AgentKey, EnvironmentKey, EndpointKey, SessionKey, and ProviderJobKey now contain only durable identity coordinates
  + purpose, program set, maximum authority, adapter profile, instance descriptor, policy, endpoint generation, locator, and sharing policy now belong to immutable revisions
  + agent and session lifecycle, cursor selection, active binding, and transition position now belong to immutable ordered snapshots
  + cursors are immutable references without mutable disposition
  + BindingClaim binds stable keys to exact revision and snapshot digests rather than nested mutable records
  + TransitionRecord makes predecessor, sequence, causation, authority, and proof explicit
  + global uniqueness, exclusive endpoint ownership, physical availability, physical binding, and effects remain later authoritative proofs
  = conclusion: normal configuration and lifecycle changes no longer create incompatible content under one stable identity record

& [DataDesignAudit] passes at conceptual and logical level
  + [natural_identity] is stable key continuity across revision and snapshot changes
  + [surrogate_identity] is UUID identity for definitions, snapshots, transitions, claims, and provider jobs
  + [content_identity] is digest binding for immutable definitions, revisions, snapshots, cursors, and claims
  + [ownership] is each revision or snapshot owns its fields and references predecessors by digest rather than duplicating mutable authority
  + [cardinality] is one current definition and runtime snapshot per admitted agent lineage, zero or one active session per current agent snapshot, one agent and endpoint per session, and many historical immutable snapshots
  + [ordering] is exact predecessor digest plus monotonic sequence rather than wall-clock inference
  + [lifecycle] is one-way, terminal sessions do not reopen, and resume creates a new predecessor-linked SessionKey
  + [provenance] is commissioning, causation, authority, source, definition, snapshot, and proof references
  + [physical_design] is deliberately absent until persistence and adapter evidence justify it

& [AuthorityAndSecurityAudit] passes for source processing
  + AgentDefinitionRevision maximum authority is a ceiling and SessionSnapshot authority is a contained projection
  + current Phase 1 EffectBroker identity exists but exterior effect classes remain denied
  + ClaimOnly records cannot mint adapter admission, endpoint availability, exclusivity, physical embodiment, or effect capability
  + provider replacement cannot change agent identity or inherit authority outside the exact agent and session projections
  + cross-agent, cross-environment, stale-revision, stale-snapshot, replay, fork, collision, and invalid-transition cases have explicit negative-proof obligations
  + no secret, credential, player identity, network endpoint, or opaque adapter locator content must enter public proof output

& [ImplementationFeasibilityAudit] passes without selecting code
  + current SemanticId and ContentDigest patterns can inform later stable-key and digest forms
  + current ParticipantAddress and AuthorityGrant demonstrate exact role-address and subset containment but do not already implement embodied identity
  + current RuntimeGeneration demonstrates shared immutable semantic substrate but has no session or per-agent state
  + safe Rust strict serde and deterministic validation are plausible under current repository patterns
  + no dependency, unsafe block, platform API, process, network, filesystem, clock, database, model, or adapter is required for the candidate pure-form slice
  + exact module, public visibility, constructors, canonical encoding, digest input grammar, registry boundary, and persistence remain SJS design questions rather than source contradictions

& [RequirementAudit] passes
  + [requirement_set] is CEA1-001 through CEA1-014
  + [atomicity] is each candidate requirement has one independently testable obligation class
  + [coverage] is identity, revision, state, cursors, claims, lifecycle, containment, proof-grade separation, multiplexing, provider attribution, faults, negative proof, non-effects, and durable traceability
  + [conflicts] are none after applying the corrective source
  + [source_revision_required] is false after correction

& [OpenSJSQuestions] are nonblocking refinement work
  + exact stable-key and record naming
  + whether initial transition sequence is zero or one
  + canonical profile strings and serialization grammar
  + digest algorithm reuse and exact digest subjects
  + whether agent-current-state admission needs a pure lineage validator separate from later persistence
  + constructor visibility that preserves inspectability without implying production provenance
  + complete closed fault ordering and rollback shape
  = must: resolve or explicitly defer these during delineation, semantic refinement, constraint checking, pruning, and data design

